  "articleBody": "Thinking about tackling that floor tile project yourself? That's awesome! But before you jump in, here are a few common mistakes folks make that you definitely want to steer clear of to get a result you'll love.\n\n1.  **Installing over an unprepared or uneven surface:** You might be tempted to skip leveling, but an uneven subfloor is a recipe for disaster. Your tiles will look lumpy and could even crack. Make sure your base is flat and solid!\n2.  **Poor alignment or lippage:** This is when your tiles aren't perfectly aligned, creating little ridges where one tile is higher than its neighbor. It's a dead giveaway of an amateur job and can be a tripping hazard. Take your time with spacers and straight lines.\n3.  **Weak adhesion from improper mixing:** Mortar isn't just 'mix and go.' If it's too watery or too thick, your tiles won't stick properly, leading to loose tiles down the road. Follow the manufacturer's instructions to a T.\n4.  **Skipping details that prevent cracking or detachment:** Things like waterproofing in wet areas or proper movement joints are super important for preventing future problems. Don't cut corners here; these small steps protect your investment. If you're unsure about any of these steps, especially for tricky areas like bathrooms or if you're using large or natural stone tiles, bringing in a pro can prevent costly fixes later. They've got the experience to make sure it's done right.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}